146	1	1bcff51f218b	/projects/talavo	625	Double haptic feedback on tab icon when no tabs open	Double haptic feedback on tab icon when no tabs open	merged	\N	doohub/issue-625-double-haptic-feedback-on-tab-icon-when-	626	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/626	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 19:48:09.709391+00	2026-03-08 20:20:31.759539+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:10.699267+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:10.744518+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=READY\\n\\nIssue #625 has no dependencies, blockers, or references to other issues. It's a standalone feature request to add double haptic feedback on the tab icon when no tabs are open.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 13.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:10.788978+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:24.418960+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:24.467245+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:24.514207+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue is straightforward: when no tabs are open, tapping the tab icon on the homescreen should trigger double haptic feedback (instead of single or none) to indicate the empty state.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 10.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:24.558084+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:35.492244+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:35.538822+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:35.581374+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=PR created: https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/626\\n\\n**What changed** — in `bottom_toolbar.dart`, when `count == 0` the tab icon's `onTap` was `null` (no feedback). Now it fires two `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` calls 100ms apart to give a distinct \\"empty\\" double-tap feel.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 122.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:48:35.625555+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:50:37.823480+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan — #625 Double Haptic Feedback on Tab Icon (Already Implemented)\\n\\n### Summary\\nWhen no tabs are open (`count == 0`), the tab icon's `onTap` was `null`, giving no feedback. The fix provides a double haptic pulse to signal \\"empty.\\"\\n\\n### File Modified\\n- **`app/lib/features/home/presentation/widgets/bottom_toolbar.dart`** (line ~123)\\n\\n### Change\\n- **Before:** `onTap: null` when `count == 0` — icon was completely unresponsive\\n- **After:** `onTap` fires an async callback that:\\n  1. Calls `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()`\\n  2. Waits 100ms (`Future.delayed`)\\n  3. Calls `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` again\\n\\n### Why This Works\\n- Two `lightImpact()` calls 100ms apart produce a distinct double-tap feel, distinguishable from the single haptic on a normal tab open\\n- `lightImpact` is the lightest available feedback — appropriate for a \\"nothing here\\" signal\\n- No navigation or state change occurs, just tactile feedback\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Considerations\\n- **Rapid tapping:** No debounce, but since the callback only triggers haptics (no state mutation), rapid taps are harmless — worst case is overlapping vibrations\\n- **Platform differences:** `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` is a no-op on platforms without haptic engines (e.g. some Android devices, desktop). No crash risk.\\n- **100ms delay:** Short enough to feel like a single \\"double-tap\\" gesture, not two separate events. This is a reasonable value but is subjective — could be tuned (80–150ms range)\\n\\n### No Other Files Affected\\n- No new imports needed (`HapticFeedback` was already imported)\\n- No new widgets or utilities created\\n- No dead code introduced", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 24.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:50:37.876740+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:02.670326+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=The implementation is already complete and the PR is open. The change correctly adds double haptic feedback (two `lightImpact()` calls 100ms apart) when tapping the tab icon with no tabs open.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/626", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 16.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:02.722999+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:18.785347+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The change is straightforward and correct. It replaces the `null` onTap handler (when no tabs are open) with a double haptic feedback using a 100ms delay between pulses.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation is clean and matches the issue requirements. The 100ms delay between haptic pulses is a reasonable interval to ensure both are perceptible. No edge cases or issues to flag., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 13.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:18.835440+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:32.648170+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:32.700518+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:32.748132+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #625 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 202.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:32.796376+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:51:32.796382+00:00"}]	\N
