_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.721394+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.765382+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=The file is small and the fix is clear. Here's the context summary:\\n\\n## Project Context\\n\\n**Relevant file:** `backend/app/core/fcm.py:19` — contains the sole `send_push()` function.\\n\\n**Current state:** The `messaging.Message` on line 27 has `token`, `notification`, and `data` fields but no `apns` field. iOS devices need `APNSConfig` → `APNSPayload` → `Aps(sound=\\"default\\")` to trigger alert sounds.\\n\\n**Coding patterns/conventions:**\\n- All needed classes (`APNSConfig`, `APNSPayload`, `Aps`) are already available via the existing `from firebase_admin import credentials, messaging` import — no new dependencies needed.\\n- The fix is purely additive: add an `apns=` kwarg to the existing `messaging.Message(...)` constructor call.\\n- The function signature and logging pattern stay unchanged.\\n\\n**No other files need changes.** This is a single-function, single-file fix.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.808030+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:16.982995+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n**File:** `backend/app/core/fcm.py` — modify the `messaging.Message()` call in `send_push()` (~line 27)\\n\\n**What to do:** Add an `apns` keyword argument to the existing `messaging.Message(...)` constructor:\\n\\n- Add `apns=messaging.APNSConfig(payload=messaging.APNSPayload(aps=messaging.Aps(sound=\\"default\\")))` as a new kwarg alongside the existing `token`, `notification`, and `data` args.\\n\\n### No other changes needed\\n\\n- No new imports — `APNSConfig`, `APNSPayload`, `Aps` are all on `firebase_admin.messaging`, already imported.\\n- No new files, no test changes, no config changes.\\n\\n### Edge cases / risks\\n\\n- **Android unaffected** — `APNSConfig` is iOS-only; Android ignores it, so no regression risk.\\n- **Sound value** — `\\"default\\"` is the standard iOS system sound. Custom sounds would require the sound file bundled in the app; `\\"default\\"` is the correct choice here.\\n- **Silent/DND** — iOS respects user device settings regardless of this field, so no concern about overriding user preferences.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:17.032792+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:29.727016+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/185", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 31.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:29.774226+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:01.387621+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The change is clean and correct. The fix adds the standard APNS sound configuration (`\\"default\\"`) to the FCM `Message` object, which is the correct way to enable notification sounds on iOS via the Firebase Admin SDK.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation:\\n- Uses the correct `messaging.APNSConfig` / `APNSPayload` / `Aps` nesting from the Firebase Admin SDK\\n- `sound=\\"default\\"` is the standard value for playing the device's default notification sound on iOS\\n- No Android-side change is needed since Android uses the notification channel's sound setting by default\\n- The change is minimal and focused on the issue\\n- Existing error handling and guard clauses remain intact, review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 20.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:01.436197+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:21.900202+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "n