"check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 8.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:29:20.149727+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:29:28.977309+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:29:29.025736+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:29:29.069218+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=Now I have all the context needed. Here's the project context summary for implementing issue #200:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project Context: Issue #200 — Resolve Conflicts → Start Claude Session\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `app/lib/pipelines/view/pipeline_detail_screen.dart:341-365` | **Flutter**: \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" button — currently calls `launchUrl(Uri.parse('$prUrl/conflicts'))` |\\n| `web/src/components/pipeline-card.tsx:124-130` | **Web**: \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" button in pipeline list cards — `<a href={prConflictsUrl}>` |\\n| `web/src/app/pipelines/[key]/page.tsx:286-291` | **Web**: \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" button in pipeline detail — same `<a href>` pattern |\\n| `app/lib/sessions/bloc/sessions_cubit.dart:137-147` | **Flutter**: `createSession(projectPath, model)` → returns `session_key` |\\n| `app/lib/services/api.dart` | **Flutter**: `api.createSession({model, projectPath})` — POSTs to `/sessions` |\\n| `web/src/components/create-session-dialog.tsx:57-80` | **Web**: `apiFetch(\\"/sessions\\", {POST, {model, project_path}})` pattern |\\n| `web/src/app/sessions/page.tsx:34` | **Web**: After create → `router.push('/sessions/${key}')` navigation pattern |\\n| `backend/app/routers/sessions.py:51-68` | **Backend**: `POST /sessions` — creates session with `project_path`, `model`, `name` |\\n| `backend/app/schemas/session.py` | **Backend**: `CreateSessionRequest` — fields: `name`, `model`, `project_path` |\\n| `app/lib/models/pipeline.dart` | **Flutter**: `Pipeline` model — has `repoPath`, `model`, `branch`, `prUrl`, `prNumber` |\\n\\n### Current Conflict Resolution Flow\\n1. Backend `GET /pipelines/{key}/merge-status` returns `has_conflicts: bool`\\n2. UI checks `mergeStatus.has_conflicts` → shows orange \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" button\\n3. Button opens `$prUrl/conflicts` in browser (GitHub conflict editor) — **this is what changes**\\n\\n### How Claude Sessions Are Created (Pattern to Reuse)\\n\\n**Backend**: `POST /sessions` with `{ model, project_path, name? }` → returns `{ session_key, name }`\\n\\n**Flutter** (in `PipelineDetailScreen` context):\\n```dart\\nfinal sessionKey = await context.read<SessionsCubit>().createSession(\\n  projectPath: pipeline.repoPath,\\n  model: pipeline.model,\\n);\\ncontext.push('/sessions/$sessionKey');\\n```\\n\\n**Web** (in pipeline detail/card context):\\n```typescript\\nconst res = await apiFetch(\\"/sessions\\", {\\n  method: \\"POST\\",\\n  body: JSON.stringify({ model: pipeline.model, project_path: pipeline.repo_path }),\\n});\\nconst { session_key } = await res.json();\\nrouter.push(`/sessions/${session_key}`);\\n```\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **The `SessionsCubit` is not necessarily provided in the `PipelineDetailScreen` widget tree.** The cubit may need to be accessed via `context.read<SessionsCubit>()` if it's registered at the app level, or the raw `ApiService` can be used directly. Check the BLoC provider setup in `router.dart` or the main app widget.\\n\\n2. **Initial prompt**: The session will open blank — to fulfill the issue's goal of \\"analyzes conflicts and resolves them automatically,\\" the implementation should either:\\n   - Navigate to the session and have the user type the prompt (simpler), OR\\n   - Send an initial message immediately after session creation (look at `POST /sessions/{key}/messages` for the message-sending API)\\n\\n3. **Pipeline has `repoPath` and `branch`**: both available in `Pipeline` model, so the session can be pre-targeted to the right repo.\\n\\n4. **`CreateSessionRequest.project_path` is required** (not optional in the schema), so always pass `pipeline.repoPath`.\\n\\n5. **Web pipeline detail page** uses `useRouter()` from `next/navigation` for navigation — follow that pattern.\\n\\n6. **Web pipeline card** (`pipeline-card.tsx`) is a shared component used in the list view; it currently uses `e.stopPropagation()` on merge buttons — do the same for the resolve conflicts button to prevent card click-through.\\n\\n7. **Backend**: No changes needed — existing `POST /sessions` endpoint is sufficient. A follow-up could add an initial message send after session creation, but that's optional.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 162.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:29:29.113505+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:32:11.180419+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=# Implementation Plan: Issue #200 — Resolve Conflicts → Start Claude Session\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nReplace the \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" browser link with a button that creates a new Claude session pre-targeted at the pipeline's repo, then navigates the user to that session. Optionally send an initial prompt instructing Claude to resolve the merge conflicts on the branch.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Changes by Component\\n\\n### 1. Flutter App — `app/lib/pipelines/view/pipeline_detail_screen.dart`\\n\\n**Lines ~341-365** — Replace the `launchUrl` call with session creation + navigation:\\n\\n- Import `SessionsCubit` (or use `ApiService` directly if the cubit isn't in the widget tree)\\n- On \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" tap:\\n  1. Call `api.createSession(projectPath: pipeline.repoPath, model: pipeline.model, name: \\"Resolve conflicts: ${pipeline.branch}\\")`\\n  2. Navigate to `/sessions/$sessionKey`\\n  3. Optionally: send an initial message via `POST /sessions/{key}/messages` with a prompt like: `\\"Resolve the merge conflicts on branch '${pipeline.branch}'. Fix all conflicts, commit, and push.\\"`\\n- Add loading state (disable button, show spinner) while session is being created\\n- Handle errors (show snackbar on failure)\\n\\n**Check needed**: Verify whether `SessionsCubit` is available in the pipeline detail widget tree. If not, use `ApiService` directly via `context.read<ApiService>()`.\\n\\n### 2. Web — Pipeline Detail Page — `web/src/app/pipelines/[key]/page.tsx`\\n\\n**Lines ~286-291** — Replace the `<a href={prConflictsUrl}>` with an onClick handler:\\n\\n- Change from `<a>` link to `<button>` (or `<a>` with `onClick` + `e.preventDefault()`)\\n- On click:\\n  1. `apiFetch(\\"/sessions\\", { method: \\"POST\\", body: { model: pipeline.model, project_path: pipeline.repo_path, name: \\"Resolve conflicts: ${pipeline.branch}\\" } })`\\n  2. `router.push(`/sessions/${session_key}`)`\\n- Add loading state (disabled + spinner while creating)\\n- Use `useRouter()` already available in the component\\n\\n### 3. Web — Pipeline Card — `web/src/components/pipeline-card.tsx`\\n\\n**Lines ~124-130** — Same pattern as detail page:\\n\\n- Replace `<a href={prConflictsUrl}>` with a button/onClick handler\\n- Use `e.stopPropagation()` (already done for merge buttons — follow same pattern)\\n- Create session → navigate to `/sessions/${session_key}`\\n- Add loading state\\n\\n### 4. Backend — No changes required\\n\\nThe existing `POST /sessions` endpoint handles everything needed. The `project_path`, `model`, and `name` fields are sufficient.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Optional Enhancement: Auto-send Initial Prompt\\n\\nAfter creating the session, immediately send a first message so Claude starts working on conflicts without the user needing to type anything:\\n\\n- **Endpoint**: `POST /sessions/{key}/messages` (verify this exists)\\n- **Prompt**: `\\"There are merge conflicts on branch '${branch}'. Please resolve all conflicts, commit the resolution, and push to the branch.\\"`\\n- This could be done client-side right after session creation, before navigation\\n- If this endpoint doesn't exist or the UX feels wrong, skip — the user can type the prompt manually\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n1. **Session creation failure** — Network error or backend down. Show error toast, don't navigate away.\\n2. **Race condition on card click** — User double-clicks. Disable button immediately on first click.\\n3. **SessionsCubit availability (Flutter)** — May not be in the widget tree for pipeline screens. Fall back to raw API call if needed.\\n4. **Pipeline missing `repoPath`** — Shouldn't happen if there are conflicts, but guard against null.\\n5. **Session name uniqueness** — Not enforced by backend, so including branch name is just for UX clarity.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files Summary\\n\\n| File | Action |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `app/lib/pipelines/view/pipeline_detail_screen.dart` | Modify — replace `launchUrl` with session creation + navigation |\\n| `web/src/app/pipelines/[key]/page.tsx` | Modify — replace `<a>` link with onClick session creation |\\n| `web/src/components/pipeline-card.tsx` | Modify — replace `<a>` link with onClick session creation |\\n\\n**No new files needed. No backend changes needed.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n\\n1. Web pipeline detail page (easiest to test, most used)\\n2. Web pipeline card\\n3. Flutter app\\n4. (Optional) Add initial prompt auto-send", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 29.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:32:11.227411+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:32:40.979204+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/201", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 294.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:32:41.026463+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:37:35.245335+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=APPROVED\\n\\nThe implementation is clean and matches the requirements well. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n**What it does:** Replaces the \\"Resolve Conflicts\\" link (which opened the GitHub conflicts page) with a button that creates a new Claude session and navigates to it — in both the Flutter app and the Next.js web app (list view and detail view).\\n\\n**Reviewed areas:**\\n\\n- **Logic:** Correct across all three surfaces (Flutter detail, web list, web detail). Loading state is properly tracked and reset on error. The `mounted` check in Flutter prevents setState-after-dispose.\\n- **State management:** The `resolvingConflicts` flag is added as an optional boolean to `MergeStatus` (backward-compatible). State is set optimistically and cleaned up in catch blocks.\\n- **Navigation:** Both platforms navigate to the new session after creation. The Flutter version uses `context.push`, web uses `router.push`.\\n- **Error handling:** Flutter shows a SnackBar on failure. Web silently resets the loading state (consistent with how merge errors are handled elsewhere in the same codebase).\\n- **Event propagation:** `e.stopPropagation()` is preserved on the card button to prevent navigating to the pipeline detail when clicking the button.\\n- **No duplicate `handleResolveConflicts` logic concern:** The web list page and detail page both need independent handlers since they live in different components — this is expected.\\n\\nNo bugs, security issues, or missing edge cases found., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 38.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:37:35.297665+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:38:14.043259+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:38:14.090045+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:38:14.133522+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #200 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 544.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T20:38:14.179322+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T20:38:14.179327+00:00"}]	\N
