ted", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:34.586116+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:34.629538+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary: Issue #615\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `app/lib/features/browser/presentation/widgets/video_overlay.dart:64` | **Bug location** — hardcoded `screenSize.width * 9 / 16 + 28` drag area height |\\n| `app/lib/features/browser/presentation/screens/browser_screen.dart:622–631` | Drag handlers (`_onVideoVerticalDragUpdate`, `_onVideoVerticalDragEnd`) and VideoOverlay instantiation (line 1479) |\\n| `app/lib/features/browser/data/browser_scripts.dart` | JS injection patterns — all YouTube/video JS lives here |\\n| `app/lib/features/browser/data/script_injector.dart` | Orchestrates JS injection at page-start and page-finish |\\n| `app/lib/features/browser/data/video_utils.dart` | Video URL detection utilities (no aspect ratio logic) |\\n| `app/lib/core/constants/app_constants.dart` | `kMiniPlayerHeight = 64.0`, `kBottomBarHeight = 57.0` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### JS ↔ Flutter Communication Pattern\\n\\nThe codebase uses `flutter_inappwebview` with named handlers:\\n\\n**Flutter side** (registered in `_onVideoWebViewCreated` ~line 768):\\n```dart\\ncontroller.addJavaScriptHandler(handlerName: 'zvVideoDetected', callback: ...)\\ncontroller.addJavaScriptHandler(handlerName: 'zvMuteChanged', callback: ...)\\n// etc.\\n```\\n\\n**JS side** (in browser_scripts.dart):\\n```javascript\\nwindow.flutter_inappwebview.callHandler('zvVideoDetected', data);\\n```\\n\\nExisting handlers: `zvVideoDetected`, `zvAdBlocked`, `zvMuteChanged`, `zvPipChanged`, `zvVideoTabNav`, `zvForwardToBrowse`. A new `zvVideoAspectRatio` handler can be added following the same pattern.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Technical Observations\\n\\n1. **The `+28` magic number** — status bar/padding offset that shouldn't be needed since the video WebView already starts below `statusBarHeight` (line 53). Likely a compensating hack that should be removed or replaced.\\n\\n2. **JS can access video dimensions**: `document.querySelector('video').videoWidth` / `.videoHeight` are standard DOM properties available immediately once the video loads. `getBoundingClientRect()` gives rendered dimensions.\\n\\n3. **VideoOverlay receives drag height via constructor** — the widget itself is simple; height is passed in as a calculation. The state that needs to change lives in `BrowserScreen`, which owns the WebView controller and can register new JS handlers.\\n\\n4. **Mini player thumbnail** (line 245) also uses `16/9` hardcoded — cosmetic issue, lower priority but easy to fix with the same aspect ratio value once it's tracked.\\n\\n5. **Script injection timing** — YouTube loads the video element asynchronously. The JS detection script needs to listen for the `loadedmetadata` event (or poll), not just run once at page load.\\n\\n6. **State management** — `BrowserScreen` is a `StatefulWidget` with `setState`. The aspect ratio can be stored as a `double? _videoAspectRatio` field and passed to `VideoOverlay`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Coding Conventions to Follow\\n\\n- Dart format: run `dart format .` before committing\\n- Commit prefix: `#615 <message>`\\n- Constants go in `app_constants.dart`\\n- JS scripts added to `browser_scripts.dart` as static string methods\\n- No external packages needed — this uses only existing `flutter_inappwebview` APIs", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 97.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:34.674885+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:12.304324+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan for #615\\n\\n### Approach\\n\\nQuery the video element's rendered height via JavaScript (`getBoundingClientRect().height`) and pass it to Flutter via a new `zvVideoSize` handler. Store the height in `BrowserScreen` state and pass it to `VideoOverlay` to size the drag area dynamically. Fall back to 16:9 when no data is available yet.\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n\\n#### 1. `browser_scripts.dart` — Add aspect ratio reporting script\\n\\n- Add a new static const `videoSizeReporter` script\\n- Uses `MutationObserver` + `loadedmetadata`/`resize` events to detect the video element and report its rendered height\\n- Calls `window.flutter_inappwebview.callHandler('zvVideoSize', rect.height)` whenever the video's bounding rect height changes\\n- Also listens for `resize` event on the video element (YouTube changes video size on quality/aspect changes)\\n- Guards with `window.__zv_size_reporter` to prevent double-injection\\n\\n#### 2. `browser_screen.dart` — Store video height and wire up handler\\n\\n- Add state field: `double? _videoPlayerHeight`\\n- In `_onVideoWebViewCreated` (~line 768): register new `zvVideoSize` handler that calls `setState(() => _videoPlayerHeight = args[0])` \\n- Reset `_videoPlayerHeight = null` when a new video loads (in `_openVideoPlayer` or `_onVideoPageStarted`)\\n- Pass `_videoPlayerHeight` to `VideoOverlay` constructor\\n- In `_onVideoVerticalDragUpdate` (line 622): replace `_kDIExpandedHeight` with the actual video area height when available (computed from `_videoPlayerHeight + statusBarHeight`)\\n\\n#### 3. `video_overlay.dart` — Accept dynamic height\\n\\n- Add `double? videoPlayerHeight` parameter to `VideoOverlay` constructor\\n- Replace line 64's hardcoded `screenSize.width * 9 / 16 + 28` with:\\n  ```\\n  (videoPlayerHeight ?? screenSize.width * 9 / 16) + statusBarHeight\\n  ```\\n- The `+ 28` magic number is replaced by `statusBarHeight` — the actual padding offset — since the gesture detector starts at `top: 0` but the video starts at `statusBarHeight` (line 53)\\n\\n#### 4. `script_injector.dart` — Inject the new script\\n\\n- Add `videoSizeReporter` to the video WebView's page-finish injection list (alongside `autoUnmute`, `mediaSessionOverride`, etc.)\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **Script timing**: The video element may not exist immediately. Use `MutationObserver` (same pattern as `autoUnmute`) to wait for it, then attach event listeners.\\n- **SPA navigations**: When YouTube navigates between videos (SPA), the video element may be reused with a different aspect ratio. Listen for `loadedmetadata` on the video element to re-report dimensions.\\n- **Null safety**: Before the JS reports dimensions, fall back to 16:9 calculation so the drag area works on first load.\\n- **Shorts (9:16)**: The reported height will be larger than 16:9, making the drag area taller — correct behavior since the video fills more vertical space.\\n- **Fullscreen/rotation**: `getBoundingClientRect()` returns the current rendered size, so rotation is handled automatically as long as the script re-fires on resize.\\n- **Non-YouTube sites**: The script should work on any site with a `<video>` element. If no video is found, no handler fires and the fallback is used.\\n- **The `_kDIExpandedHeight` in drag range calculation** (line 626): This constant is for the Dynamic Island expanded height, not the video height. It may need adjustment too if the drag range should account for actual video height — investigate whether this affects drag sensitivity.\\n\\n### Execution Order\\n\\n1. Add `videoSizeReporter` script to `browser_scripts.dart`\\n2. Add handler + state to `browser_screen.dart`\\n3. Update `video_overlay.dart` to accept and use dynamic height\\n4. Add injection call in `script_injector.dart`\\n5. Run `dart format .`\\n6. Test with 16:9, 4:3, 21:9, and 9:16 (Shorts) videos", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 40.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:12.350013+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:53.067858+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/624", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 107.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:53.125429+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:41:40.589524+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=I've reviewed the full diff and the key files. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n## Review Summary\\n\\n**The core fix for #615** is well-implemented:\\n\\n- **`videoSizeReporter` JS script** (`browser_scripts.dart:587-627`): Correctly uses `getBoundingClientRect().height` to get the actual rendered video height, with `ResizeObserver` + `MutationObserver` + `loadedmetadata`/`resize` events to handle all cases (initial load, aspect ratio changes, SPA navigation). The deduplication via `lastH` prevents unnecessary callbacks.\\n\\n- **`zvVideoSize` handler** (`browser_screen.dart:800-809`): Properly guarded with `mounted`, type-safe cast via `num`, and only calls `setState` when the value actually changes.\\n\\n- **Drag area height** (`video_overlay.dart:66-68`): `(videoPlayerHeight ?? screenSize.width * 9 / 16) + statusBarHeight` — good fallback to 16:9 until the JS reports the real height, and replacing the hardcoded `28` with `statusBarHeight` is correct.\\n\\n- **Reset on new video** (`browser_screen.dart:482`): `_videoPlayerHeight = null` when opening a new video ensures stale values don't persist.\\n\\n**Other changes in the branch** (idleDismiss hardening, mini player hiding on non-video sites, bottom bar border radius removal) are from separate merged PRs and look fine.\\n\\nNo bugs, security issues, or missing edge cases found.\\n\\n**APPROVED**, review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 50.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:41:40.638191+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:42:30.843558+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:42:30.891125+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:42:30.936470+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #615 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 317.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:42:30.984472+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:42:30.984477+00:00"}]	\N
