128	2	c6f8f9c1b999	/projects/talavo	612	Regression: Video paused. Continue watching? popup came back	Regression: Video paused. Continue watching? popup came back	done	\N	doohub/issue-612-regression-video-paused-continue-watchin	613	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/613	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 14:08:54.604549+00	2026-03-08 14:11:45.837315+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:55.729070+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:55.786980+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=Issue #612 has no \\"blocked by\\", \\"depends on\\", or dependency keywords. It's a self-contained regression fix with clear, isolated scope.\\n\\n**READY**", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 9.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:55.854543+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:05.557240+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:05.604474+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:05.651496+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue identifies the exact files, line numbers, root cause, and fix needed. The acceptance criteria are specific and testable.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 5.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:05.695175+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.799226+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.845888+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.891078+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=Here's the concise project context for implementing issue #612:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project Context for Issue #612\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/browser/presentation/screens/browser_screen.dart`**\\n- **Browse WebView** (`_TabWebView.build()`, lines 1627–1654): The `initialUserScripts` list includes `visibilityOverride`, `disableAutoplay`, `videoLinkInterceptor`, `colorSchemeOverride`, and conditional ad-block scripts — but **no `idleDismiss`**.\\n- **Video WebView** (lines 1796–1803): Has `idleDismiss` already injected at `AT_DOCUMENT_START`.\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/browser/data/browser_scripts.dart`**\\n- Line 449–458: Defines `BrowserScripts.idleDismiss` — no changes needed here.\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/pip/data/pip_scripts.dart`**\\n- PiP uses `pipUnblocker`, `requestPipScript`, `exitPipScript`, `pipEventListenersScript`. **No `idleDismiss` present, but the `pipUnblocker` script is only injected when PiP is enabled via the video WebView** — so the video WebView's existing `idleDismiss` covers it. No change needed here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Coding Patterns to Follow\\n\\n- All user scripts follow the same pattern:\\n  ```dart\\n  UserScript(\\n    source: BrowserScripts.scriptName,\\n    injectionTime: UserScriptInjectionTime.AT_DOCUMENT_START,\\n  ),\\n  ```\\n- Scripts use `window.__zv_*` guards (e.g., `window.__zv_idle_dismiss`) to prevent double-injection — safe to inject in multiple WebViews.\\n- Conditional scripts use `if (condition) ...[ UserScript(...) ]` spread syntax.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Fix Summary\\n\\n**One-liner change** in `browser_screen.dart` at line 1653 (just before the closing `]` of browse WebView's `initialUserScripts`): add `idleDismiss` the same way the video WebView does at line 1800–1803.\\n\\n- **PiP**: No change needed. PiP mode renders within the video WebView which already has `idleDismiss`.\\n- **Guard**: `window.__zv_idle_dismiss` already prevents any double-injection side effects.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 77.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.935693+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:28.195391+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan for Issue #612\\n\\n### Change Required\\n\\n**Single file modification:** `app/lib/features/browser/presentation/screens/browser_screen.dart`\\n\\n### Specific Change\\n\\nIn `_TabWebView.build()` (around lines 1627–1654), add `idleDismiss` to the browse WebView's `initialUserScripts` list:\\n\\n- **Where:** After the last existing `UserScript` entry in the browse WebView's `initialUserScripts` array (before the closing `]`, around line 1653)\\n- **What:** Add a new `UserScript` entry for `BrowserScripts.idleDismiss` with `AT_DOCUMENT_START` injection time\\n- **Pattern:** Same as the existing entry in the video WebView at line 1800–1803\\n\\n### Files NOT Changed\\n\\n- `browser_scripts.dart` — script definition is correct as-is\\n- `pip_scripts.dart` — PiP runs inside the video WebView which already has `idleDismiss`\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **None meaningful.** The `__zv_idle_dismiss` guard prevents double-injection, so even if the same page context gets the script from both browse and video WebViews, it's harmless.\\n- The script runs at `AT_DOCUMENT_START`, matching the pattern used by the video WebView — this ensures it's in place before YouTube's idle detection initializes.\\n\\n### Verification\\n\\n- Play a video inline in the browse/feed tab, leave it idle — popup should not appear\\n- Play a video in the dedicated video player — should still work (existing behavior)\\n- PiP mode — should still work (covered by video WebView)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 11.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:28.262469+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:40.127610+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/613", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 30.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:40.177332+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:10.193377+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The `idleDismiss` script was already present in the video WebView (line 1805) before this PR. The PR adds it to the **browse** WebView as well (line 1645). This makes sense — the \\"Video paused. Continue watching?\\" popup is triggered by YouTube's idle detection via `window._lact`, and it could appear in the browse WebView too if a video is playing there.\\n\\nLet me verify the script logic is sound.\\n\\nThe `idleDismiss` script (lines 451-458 of `browser_scripts.dart`):\\n- Uses a guard (`__zv_idle_dismiss`) to prevent double-injection\\n- Defines `_lact` as a property with a getter returning `Date.now()` and a no-op setter\\n- Uses `Object.defineProperty` to make it non-writable by YouTube's code\\n\\nThe approach is correct — YouTube checks `window._lact` to determine when the user was last active. By making the getter always return `Date.now()`, YouTube thinks the user is always active, preventing the idle popup.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe change is minimal, correct, and consistent with the existing codebase. The `idleDismiss` script was already proven working in the video WebView — this PR simply extends it to the browse WebView where the same popup regression was occurring. The guard pattern (`__zv_idle_dismiss`) is consistent with all other scripts in `BrowserScripts`. No issues found., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 35.4, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:10.243529+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.642625+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.689330+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.733697+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #612 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 170.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.781083+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.781096+00:00"}]	\N
131	1	6e33f2714a14	/projects/Doohub	179	Add graph validation for pipeline templates	Add graph validation for pipeline templates	done	\N	doohub/issue-179-add-graph-validation-for-pipeline-templa	192	https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/192	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 16:13:05.500606+00	2026-03-08 16:19:09.938016+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:06.286686+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:06.334011+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=Issue #179 has no \\"blocked by\\", \\"depends on\\", or similar dependency language. It references building a Development Pipeline template as context for why the validation was designed, but that's background context — not a blocker.\\n\\n**READY**\\n\\nIssue #179 is self-contained. It only extends an existing function (`_validate_definition()` in `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py`) and has no dependencies on other open issues.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 10.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:06.378551+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:16.538947+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:16.587168+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:16.635636+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue is well-specified with concrete validation checks, the exact file/function to modify, and clear acceptance criteria organized by category (structural, connectivity, reachability, node-specific).", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 5.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:16.679474+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:22.499881+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:22.552458+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:22.600185+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #179\\n\\n### Key Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py` | **Primary target** — contains `_validate_definition()` to extend |\\n| `backend/app/routers/pipeline_templates.py` | Routes that call create/update, validation is triggered via Pydantic validators |\\n| `backend/app/main.py` | Seeds default template on startup — the default template is a good reference for valid graph structure |\\n| `slave/app/graph_executor.py` | Runtime executor — shows exactly what fields the executor expects per node type |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Current Validation (already done)\\n- Required top-level keys: `version`, `name`, `nodes`, `edges`\\n- Nodes: non-empty list, each has `id` and `type`, type in `ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES`\\n- Edges: each has `from`/`to`, both reference existing node IDs\\n\\n### What Needs to Be Added (per issue)\\n\\n**Structural:**\\n- Exactly one node with `type == \\"start\\"`\\n- At least one node with `type == \\"end\\"` or `type == \\"failed\\"`\\n- Node-specific required fields:\\n  - `claude_agent`: must have `prompt_template`\\n  - `condition`: must have `condition_field` and non-empty `branches`\\n\\n**Connectivity:**\\n- `condition` node `branches` values must reference existing node IDs\\n- `condition` node `default_branch` (if present) must reference existing node ID\\n- Node `targets` field (if present) must reference existing node IDs\\n\\n**Reachability (graph traversal):**\\n- BFS/DFS from the `start` node using edges + `targets` + `branches` + `default_branch`\\n- Every node must be reachable (no orphans)\\n- Every non-terminal node (`type` not in `{\\"end\\", \\"failed\\"}`) must have at least one outgoing path\\n\\n**Cycle detection:**\\n- Detect cycles in the graph; any cycle must pass through a `condition` node that has `max_iterations` set (to prevent infinite loops)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Coding Patterns & Conventions\\n\\n- **Pure Python functions** — `_validate_definition()` is a plain function, not a class method\\n- **Pydantic `field_validator`** with `@classmethod` decorator — validation hooks into Pydantic model lifecycle\\n- **Error messages are descriptive** — include node IDs, indices, and context (e.g., `\\"Node 'foo' has invalid type...\\"`)\\n- **Raise `ValueError`** — Pydantic converts these to validation errors automatically\\n- **No external libraries** — graph traversal should use standard `collections.deque` or sets; no NetworkX\\n- **ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES** — already defined at module level as a set constant; terminal node types can be similarly defined\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reference: Default Template Structure\\nThe seeded template in `main.py` is the canonical valid example:\\n- `start` node → `claude_agent` nodes → `condition` node (with `branches`, `default_branch`, `max_iterations`) → `end` node\\n- The `condition` node creates a cycle back to `developer`, guarded by `max_iterations: 3`\\n- Edges don't include the condition's outgoing branches — those are defined in `branches`/`default_branch` on the node itself\\n\\n### Graph Traversal Note\\nThe executor's `_get_next_node()` in `slave/app/graph_executor.py` resolves next nodes from (in order): `node.targets`, edge map, then condition `branches`. The validator's reachability check must follow the same traversal logic to be consistent.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 95.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:13:22.649774+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:14:58.285752+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan for Issue #179\\n\\n### File to modify\\n**`backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py`** — extend `_validate_definition()`\\n\\nNo new files needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n#### 1. Add constants (top of file, after `ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES`)\\n\\n- `TERMINAL_NODE_TYPES = {\\"end\\", \\"failed\\"}` — reuse in reachability/dead-end checks\\n\\n#### 2. Extend `_validate_definition()` — add checks after the existing edge validation (line 48)\\n\\nOrganize as sequential validation blocks inside the same function. Each block raises `ValueError` on failure.\\n\\n**Block A: Structural checks**\\n- Count nodes with `type == \\"start\\"` — must be exactly 1\\n- Count nodes with `type in TERMINAL_NODE_TYPES` — must be >= 1\\n- For each `claude_agent` node: require `prompt_template` key (non-empty string)\\n- For each `condition` node: require `condition_field` (non-empty string) and `branches` (non-empty list or dict)\\n\\n**Block B: Connectivity / reference checks**\\n- Build `node_ids` set (already exists on line 19)\\n- For each node with `targets` list: every non-empty entry must be in `node_ids`\\n- For each `condition` node:\\n  - If `branches` is a list of `{value, target}`: each `target` must be in `node_ids`\\n  - If `branches` is a dict: each value must be in `node_ids`\\n  - If `default_branch` is set: must be in `node_ids`\\n  - If `max_iterations_target` is set: must be in `node_ids`\\n\\n**Block C: Reachability (BFS from start)**\\n- Build an adjacency map covering ALL outgoing paths per node:\\n  - Edges (`from` → `to`) via `edge_map`\\n  - `targets` list on non-condition nodes\\n  - `branches` values on condition nodes\\n  - `default_branch` on condition nodes\\n  - `max_iterations_target` on condition nodes\\n  - `next` field (legacy)\\n- BFS/DFS from the single `start` node using `collections.deque`\\n- `unreachable = node_ids - visited` — if non-empty, raise with the orphan node IDs\\n\\n**Block D: Dead-end check**\\n- For every non-terminal node (`type not in TERMINAL_NODE_TYPES`): must have at least one outgoing edge in the adjacency map built above\\n- Raise with the dead-end node IDs if any found\\n\\n**Block E: Cycle safety**\\n- Run a standard DFS cycle detection (track `in_stack` set per path)\\n- For each cycle found, collect the set of node IDs in the cycle\\n- If no node in the cycle is a `condition` node with `max_iterations` set → raise `ValueError` listing the cycle path\\n- Note: a single DFS pass can find all back-edges; for each back-edge, reconstruct the cycle path from the recursion stack\\n\\n#### 3. Add `from collections import deque` at top of file\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Adjacency map construction (detail)\\n\\n```\\nFor each node:\\n  - Add edges from edge_map (from → [to])\\n  - If node has \\"targets\\": add node_id → targets\\n  - If node is condition:\\n    - branches (list or dict) → add node_id → each target\\n    - default_branch → add node_id → default_branch\\n    - max_iterations_target → add node_id → max_iterations_target\\n  - If node has \\"next\\": add node_id → next\\n```\\n\\nThis mirrors the executor's `_get_next_node()` + `_handle_condition()` logic.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **`branches` can be list or dict** — the executor handles both formats (line 191-194 of `graph_executor.py`). The validator must too.\\n- **`failed` nodes can have outgoing targets** — the executor follows `_get_next_node()` on failed nodes (line 381). So `failed` nodes should be treated as terminal only when they have no outgoing edges. However, the issue says terminal = `end` or `failed`. Resolution: for the dead-end check, only flag non-terminal nodes. For reachability, still traverse outgoing edges from `failed` nodes so downstream nodes aren't falsely flagged as orphans.\\n- **`max_iterations_target` vs `default_branch` fallback** — the executor falls back to `default_branch` if `max_iterations_target` is missing (line 204-205). Both should be validated as references if present.\\n- **Duplicate node IDs** — not currently checked. Should add: if `len(node_ids) != len(nodes)`, raise with the duplicate IDs.\\n- **Self-loops** — a node targeting itself is a cycle. If it's not a condition with `max_iterations`, it should fail validation.\\n- **Empty `targets` with empty strings** — the executor filters empty strings from targets (line 285). The validator should do the same when building adjacency.\\n\\n### Error message format\\n\\nFollow existing pattern — include node IDs and context:\\n- `\\"Node 'review_check' is a dead end: non-terminal node with no outgoing edges\\"`\\n- `\\"Nodes not reachable from start: developer, reviewer\\"`\\n- `\\"Cycle detected without max_iterations guard: start → developer → review_check → developer\\"`\\n\\n### Testing\\n\\n- The seeded default template in `main.py` should pass all new validation (sanity check)\\n- Manual testing with malformed definitions to verify each check fires correctly\\n- Consider adding unit tests in a new `backend/tests/test_pipeline_template_validation.py` if a test directory exists", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 42.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:14:58.334713+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:15:41.262077+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/192", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 134.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:15:41.315792+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:17:56.227627+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=I've reviewed the full PR diff and source files. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n## Review Summary\\n\\n**Scope:** Backend graph validation for pipeline templates, frontend compile/validate, legacy orchestrator removal, UI improvements (context panel, edge sync, compile animation).\\n\\n### Backend Validation (`pipeline_template.py`)\\n- Thorough: duplicate IDs, exactly-one-start, terminal node presence, required fields per type, reference integrity, BFS reachability, dead-end detection, unguarded cycle detection.\\n- Adjacency builder correctly covers all edge sources: explicit edges, `targets`, `next`, `branches`, `default_branch`, `max_iterations_target`.\\n- Cycle safety DFS is sound for the expected graph sizes.\\n- Minor: `parent` dict on line 186 is declared but never used — harmless but dead code.\\n\\n### Frontend Validation (`validate-graph.ts`)\\n- Mirrors backend checks (start/terminal/reachability/dead-ends/condition fields/agent prompts).\\n- No cycle detection on frontend — acceptable since backend is authoritative.\\n- Missing newline at EOF — trivial.\\n\\n### Orchestrator (`slave/`)\\n- Clean removal of legacy plan→develop→review state machine and `agent_prompts.py`.\\n- `template_definition` correctly made required across the stack (router → client → orchestrator).\\n- PR URL auto-detection via regex in `_handle_claude_agent` is correct.\\n- `max_attempts` hardcoded to 2 matches the UI change removing retry config.\\n\\n### Edge/Node Sync (web)\\n- `scrubNodeReferences` correctly cleans up dangling references on delete.\\n- `onEdgesChange` properly syncs node config when edges are removed.\\n- `onConnect` correctly adds to node targets/branches when edges are drawn.\\n\\n### Pipeline Router\\n- `template_id` now required — consistent with the template-only approach.\\n- `issue_body` no longer pre-set from `task_description`; always fetched fresh from GitHub — correct.\\n\\n### Tests\\n- No tests for the validation logic. The project has no test infrastructure, so this is a pre-existing gap, not introduced by this PR.\\n\\n### Issues Found\\nNone blocking. The unused `parent` variable is cosmetic.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe validation logic is comprehensive and consistent across backend and frontend. The legacy orchestrator removal is clean. No bugs, security issues, or missing edge cases., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 73.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:17:56.279142+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:19:09.742004+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:19:09.792875+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:19:09.850056+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #179 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 363.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:19:09.902071+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:19:09.902080+00:00"}]	\N
