rete — clicking the button copies the template with a \\"Copy of [name]\\" naming convention, and the copy should appear immediately in the list. A developer knows what UI to add, what interaction to implement, and what the expected outcome is.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 9.1, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:32:46.932535+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:32:55.992791+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:32:56.041968+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:32:56.090479+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #202\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `web/src/components/template-card.tsx` | Template card component — needs duplicate button |\\n| `web/src/app/templates/page.tsx` | Template list page — manages state and handlers |\\n| `web/src/store/templates.ts` | Zustand store — needs `duplicateTemplate()` action |\\n| `backend/app/routers/pipeline_templates.py` | REST routes — no duplicate endpoint yet |\\n| `backend/app/models/pipeline_template.py` | DB model — `name` is unique (max 200 chars) |\\n| `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py` | Create/update schemas — used for POST body |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### UI Patterns to Follow\\n\\n**Icon buttons on cards** use `opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100` and appear on the right side:\\n```tsx\\n<Button\\n  variant=\\"ghost\\"\\n  size=\\"icon\\"\\n  className=\\"h-6 w-6 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100\\"\\n  onClick={(e) => { e.stopPropagation(); onDuplicate(); }}\\n>\\n  <Copy className=\\"h-3 w-3\\" />\\n</Button>\\n```\\n\\nThe card root has `className=\\"group ...\\"` — already set for hover behavior.\\n\\nLucide's `Copy` icon is available and fits perfectly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Store Pattern\\n\\nThe Zustand store at `templates.ts` already has `createTemplate(body)` which POSTs to `/pipeline-templates`. Duplication can reuse this — fetch the template, construct a new body with `\\"Copy of [name]\\"`, and call `createTemplate`.\\n\\nNo backend endpoint is strictly necessary — duplication can be done **entirely on the frontend** using existing create + fetch.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **Name uniqueness**: Backend enforces unique names (409 on conflict). The \\"Copy of X\\" name must be unique — may need fallback naming like \\"Copy of X (2)\\".\\n\\n2. **Definition deep copy**: The `definition` JSONB field includes nodes and edges — just spread/copy the object, no special handling needed.\\n\\n3. **No backend change required**: Since `createTemplate` already exists, the frontend can fetch the template data from the store (already in state) and POST a copy. No new backend endpoint needed.\\n\\n4. **Prop wiring**: `template-card.tsx` gets `onDelete` passed from `page.tsx`. Same pattern needed for `onDuplicate`.\\n\\n5. **Immediate availability**: After duplication, calling `fetchTemplates()` (or optimistically appending to state) will show the new template instantly.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 64.1, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:32:56.136444+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:34:00.242819+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan for Issue #202\\n\\n### Approach\\n\\nFrontend-only solution. Reuse the existing `createTemplate` store action to POST a copy with a modified name. No backend changes needed.\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n\\n#### 1. `web/src/store/templates.ts`\\n- Add a `duplicateTemplate(id: number)` action to `TemplatesState` interface\\n- Implementation:\\n  - Find the template by `id` from current `state.templates`\\n  - Build a `CreateTemplateBody` with:\\n    - `name`: `\\"Copy of {original.name}\\"` (truncated to 200 chars max)\\n    - `description`: same as original\\n    - `definition`: deep copy via `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(original.definition))`\\n  - Call `createTemplate(body)` internally\\n  - If it returns `null` (409 conflict), retry with `\\"Copy of {name} (2)\\"`, `\\"Copy of {name} (3)\\"`, etc. (up to ~3 retries)\\n  - Return the created template or `null`\\n\\n#### 2. `web/src/components/template-card.tsx`\\n- Add `Copy` to the lucide-react import\\n- Add `onDuplicate` prop (same pattern as `onDelete`)\\n- Add a duplicate button **before** the delete button:\\n  ```\\n  <Button variant=\\"ghost\\" size=\\"icon\\" className=\\"h-6 w-6 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 shrink-0\\" onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); onDuplicate(); }}>\\n    <Copy className=\\"h-3 w-3\\" />\\n  </Button>\\n  ```\\n\\n#### 3. `web/src/app/templates/page.tsx`\\n- Destructure `duplicateTemplate` from the store\\n- Add `handleDuplicate` async function that calls `duplicateTemplate(id)`\\n- Pass `onDuplicate={() => handleDuplicate(template.id)}` to each `<TemplateCard>`\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **Name uniqueness (409)**: Backend enforces unique names. The retry logic with `(2)`, `(3)` suffixes handles conflicts. Cap retries at 3 to avoid infinite loops.\\n- **Name length**: `\\"Copy of ...\\"` could exceed the 200-char limit. Truncate the base name before prefixing.\\n- **Definition copy**: Use `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify())` to avoid shared references in the JSONB definition.\\n- **No navigation after duplicate**: Unlike create, duplicating should stay on the list page (the new template just appears in the list via optimistic state update in `createTemplate`).\\n- **Loading state**: Optional — could add a brief loading indicator, but since `createTemplate` already optimistically updates the store, the UX should be instant enough without one.\\n\\n### Order of Implementation\\n\\n1. Store action (`duplicateTemplate`)\\n2. Card component (add button + prop)\\n3. Page (wire handler)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 24.8, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:34:00.298493+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:34:25.114251+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/204", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 79.8, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:34:25.165631+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:35:45.008542+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=I've reviewed the full diff and the store file. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n**Changes summary:**\\n- Adds a `duplicateTemplate` action to the Zustand store\\n- Adds a duplicate (Copy) button to the template card UI\\n- Wires it up in the templates page\\n\\n**Review:**\\n\\n1. **UI layer** — Clean. `e.stopPropagation()` correctly prevents the card click from firing. The button styling is consistent with the existing delete button pattern (ghost, icon, hover reveal).\\n\\n2. **Store logic** — The `duplicateTemplate` function deep-clones via `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))` which is appropriate for this plain data structure. Name truncation to 200 chars is handled.\\n\\n3. **Retry logic concern (minor)** — The retry loop (4 attempts with incrementing suffix) assumes `createTemplate` returning `null` means a name conflict, but `createTemplate` returns `null` for *any* API failure (network error, 500, etc.). This means it could pointlessly retry on unrelated failures. However, it's capped at 4 attempts and is a silent no-op on failure, which is consistent with the rest of the store's error handling pattern. Not a blocker.\\n\\n4. **No regressions** — `onDuplicate` is correctly typed as required (`() => void`), which is fine since it's always passed in the only call site.\\n\\n5. **Security** — No injection vectors. The definition is deep-cloned before sending to the API.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation is straightforward, consistent with existing patterns, and correctly handles the core functionality. The retry-on-any-failure behavior is a minor imperfection but not worth blocking on., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 42.7, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:35:45.064631+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:36:27.752422+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:36:27.811853+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:36:27.862557+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #202 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 232.7, "started_at": "2026-03-09T05:36:27.911260+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-09T05:36:27.911265+00:00"}]	\N
