359309+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue describes a template composition feature with sufficient detail:\\n- What: nest existing templates as nodes within other templates\\n- Why: reusability and modularity\\n- Acceptance criteria are concrete (add template as node, execute full flow, support conditional execution)\\n\\nA developer can understand what to build from this description.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 6.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:18:39.447506+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:18:45.967982+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:18:46.017942+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:18:46.064756+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #190\\n\\n### Architecture Overview\\n\\nThe project is a monorepo: **FastAPI backend** + **Next.js frontend** + **Python slave executor** + **Flutter app**.\\n\\nTemplates are stored as JSONB `definition` blobs in `pipeline_templates` table containing nodes and edges.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `backend/app/models/pipeline_template.py` | SQLAlchemy model — `definition` JSONB column holds full graph |\\n| `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py` | Pydantic validation — `ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES` list, `_validate_definition()` |\\n| `backend/app/routers/pipeline_templates.py` | CRUD API endpoints |\\n| `slave/app/graph_executor.py` | Execution engine — `execute_graph()`, node handlers |\\n| `web/src/app/templates/[id]/page.tsx` | Builder page — `nextNodeId()`, toolbar, save logic |\\n| `web/src/components/builder/toolbar.tsx` | Node type palette (currently: Agent, Condition, Done, Failed) |\\n| `web/src/components/builder/config-panel.tsx` | Right-panel node property editor |\\n| `web/src/lib/template-flow.ts` | `definitionToFlow()` / `flowToDefinition()` converters |\\n| `web/src/lib/validate-graph.ts` | Frontend graph validation |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Existing Node Types (5)\\n`start`, `end`, `failed`, `claude_agent`, `condition`\\n\\nEach node has: `id`, `type`, `name`, `position`, `targets[]`, plus type-specific fields.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### What Needs to Be Added\\n\\n**Backend:**\\n- Add `\\"template\\"` to `ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES` in schemas\\n- Validate the referenced `template_id` exists and no circular references\\n- Add `_handle_template()` in `graph_executor.py` — fetch the referenced template's definition, call `execute_graph()` recursively (or inline its nodes), propagate context/outputs back\\n\\n**Frontend:**\\n- New node renderer component (`template-node.tsx`)\\n- Add \\"Template\\" to `toolbar.tsx`\\n- Add config panel section to select which template + map inputs/outputs\\n- Update `definitionToFlow()` / `flowToDefinition()` to handle `type: \\"template\\"`\\n- Update `validate-graph.ts` to validate template references\\n- Need API call to list available templates for the picker\\n\\n**API:**\\n- When loading the builder, fetch available templates for the selector dropdown\\n- The existing `GET /pipeline-templates` endpoint can be reused\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **Circular reference prevention** — A template referencing itself or creating a cycle must be rejected at save time (backend validation)\\n2. **Context propagation** — The slave executor's `ctx` dict is shared; nested template execution must merge its outputs back into the parent context\\n3. **Node ID scoping** — When inlining a nested template's nodes during execution, their IDs must be namespaced to avoid collisions\\n4. **No input/output mapping needed initially** — Simplest implementation shares the full parent context with the nested template (same `ctx` dict)\\n5. **Conditional execution** — Already supported by existing `condition` node type; no new mechanism needed — users can gate the template node behind a condition node\\n6. **The `targets` field** — Template node needs `targets` like all other non-terminal nodes to declare what runs after it completes", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 101.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:18:46.109030+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:20:27.384967+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=# Implementation Plan: Template Nodes (Issue #190)\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nAdd a `template` node type that references another template by ID. At execution time, the slave executor fetches the referenced template's definition and runs `execute_graph()` recursively, sharing the parent's `ctx` dict. On the frontend, users pick from existing templates via a dropdown in the config panel.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1: Backend Schema & Validation\\n\\n### `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py`\\n\\n- Add `\\"template\\"` to `ALLOWED_NODE_TYPES`\\n- In `_validate_definition()`, add validation for template nodes:\\n  - Each template node must have a `template_id` (int) field\\n  - `template_id` must not equal the template's own ID (self-reference check — requires passing current template ID into validation)\\n- Update `PipelineTemplateUpdate` and `PipelineTemplateCreate` validators to accept an optional `template_id` context param for self-reference checking\\n\\n### `backend/app/routers/pipeline_templates.py`\\n\\n- In the **PUT** endpoint: pass the template's own ID into `_validate_definition()` so it can reject self-references\\n- Add a **deep circular reference check**: when saving a template that contains template nodes, recursively walk referenced templates' definitions to detect cycles (template A → B → A). This is a DB query per referenced template — acceptable since nesting depth should be small\\n- No new endpoints needed — the existing `GET /pipeline-templates` list endpoint serves as the template picker data source\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2: Executor (Slave)\\n\\n### `slave/app/graph_executor.py`\\n\\n- **New handler: `_handle_template(node, ctx)`**\\n  - Read `template_id` from `node`\\n  - Fetch the template definition from DB (need DB session access — follow existing patterns for how the executor gets DB access, or pass a template-fetcher callback into `execute_graph`)\\n  - Call `execute_graph()` recursively with the fetched definition and the **same `ctx` dict**\\n  - Namespace nested node keys: prefix `ctx` keys from the nested execution with `{node_id}.` to avoid collisions (e.g., `_raw_agent1` becomes `_raw_templateNode1.agent1`)\\n  - On nested completion: propagate success/failure status back — if nested template hits a `failed` node, the template node itself should be treated as failed\\n  - Return `None` on success (normal flow continues to targets) or handle failure routing\\n\\n- **Add to `_NODE_HANDLERS`**: `\\"template\\": _handle_template`\\n\\n- **Recursion depth guard**: Add a `depth` parameter to `execute_graph()` (default 0), increment on recursive calls, reject if `depth > 5` (configurable). This is a runtime safety net alongside the compile-time cycle check\\n\\n- **Context key scoping strategy**:\\n  - Before nested execution, snapshot `ctx` keys\\n  - After nested execution, any new keys added by the nested template get prefixed with `{parent_node_id}.` in the parent context\\n  - Special keys like `cost_usd` are additive (accumulated, not scoped)\\n  - `_end_result` and `_fail_reason` from nested execution are captured as `_raw_{node_id}` in parent context, then cleared\\n\\n- **Template fetching**: Add a `template_loader` async callback parameter to `execute_graph()`. The caller (slave main loop) provides a function that takes a template_id and returns the definition dict. This keeps the executor decoupled from DB access patterns.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 3: Frontend — Node Component\\n\\n### New file: `web/src/components/builder/template-node.tsx`\\n\\n- Follow the pattern of `agent-node.tsx` (card-style, target + source handles)\\n- Display: template name, a \\"Layers\\" or \\"Workflow\\" icon (from lucide-react)\\n- Show the referenced template's name (stored in `node.data.template_name`)\\n- Selected state: emerald ring (same as other nodes)\\n- Size: `w-52` (same as agent node)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 4: Frontend — Toolbar & Config Panel\\n\\n### `web/src/components/builder/toolbar.tsx`\\n\\n- Add `{ type: \\"template\\", label: \\"Template\\" }` to `NODE_OPTIONS` array\\n\\n### `web/src/components/builder/config-panel.tsx`\\n\\n- Add a `template` case in the node type switch:\\n  - **Template selector dropdown**: fetch templates from `GET /pipeline-templates`, show as `<select>`. Filter out the current template being edited (prevent self-reference in UI)\\n  - Store selected template's ID as `data.template_id` and name as `data.template_name`\\n  - **NextNodes** component (same as agent/start nodes for target wiring)\\n  - Status label field (optional, same as agent node)\\n\\n### `web/src/app/templates/[id]/page.tsx`\\n\\n- Register `template: TemplateNode` in the `nodeTypes` map\\n- Add `template` case in `handleAddNode` with defaults: `{ template_id: null, template_name: \\"\\", targets: [] }`\\n- Fetch available templates on page load (or lazily when config panel opens) using existing API\\n- Pass available templates list to `ConfigPanel` as a prop\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 5: Frontend — Flow Converters & Validation\\n\\n### `web/src/lib/template-flow.ts`\\n\\n- In `definitionToFlow()`: handle `type: \\"template\\"` same as agent/start/failed — populate `data.targets` from edges\\n- In `flowToDefinition()`: include `template_id` and `template_name` in the node data spread (already handled by the generic spread, but verify)\\n\\n### `web/src/lib/validate-graph.ts`\\n\\n- Add validation for template nodes:\\n  - Must have a `template_id` set (not null)\\n  - Must have at least one outgoing edge (not a terminal node)\\n  - Self-reference check: `template_id !== currentTemplateId` (pass current template ID into validator)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## File Change Summary\\n\\n| File | Action | Changes |\\n|------|--------|---------|\\n| `backend/app/schemas/pipeline_template.py` | Modify | Add `\\"template\\"` to allowed types, add `template_id` validation |\\n| `backend/app/routers/pipeline_templates.py` | Modify | Add circular reference detection on save |\\n| `slave/app/graph_executor.py` | Modify | Add `_handle_template`, depth guard, template_loader param |\\n| `web/src/components/builder/template-node.tsx` | **Create** | New node visual component |\\n| `web/src/components/builder/toolbar.tsx` | Modify | Add Template to NODE_OPTIONS |\\n| `web/src/components/builder/config-panel.tsx` | Modify | Add template config section with picker |\\n| `web/src/app/templates/[id]/page.tsx` | Modify | Register node type, add defaults, fetch templates |\\n| `web/src/lib/template-flow.ts` | Modify | Handle template type in target population |\\n| `web/src/lib/validate-graph.ts` | Modify | Add template node validation rules |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n1. **Circular references**: Two-layer protection — backend rejects cycles at save time (walks the graph), executor has depth limit at runtime\\n2. **Deleted referenced template**: If a template is deleted while another references it, execution will fail. Mitigation: update the DELETE endpoint to check for template node references (same pattern as existing pipeline reference check)\\n3. **Context key collisions**: Scoping nested keys with `{node_id}.` prefix prevents collisions but means downstream nodes in the parent can't easily reference nested outputs by simple name. This is acceptable for v1 — users can use the full scoped name\\n4. **Cost tracking**: `cost_usd` must be additive across nested calls, not overwritten. Accumulate in the shared ctx\\n5. **Step logging**: Nested execution steps should be included in the parent's step log, prefixed or grouped by the template node ID for clarity\\n6. **Template updates after embedding**: Template nodes reference by ID, so if the referenced template is updated, the next execution uses the latest version. This is the desired behavior (always run latest)\\n7. **Conditional execution**: No special work needed — users place a `condition` node before the `template` node, which is already supported\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n\\n1. **Backend schema** — add type, basic validation (quick, unblocks frontend)\\n2. **Frontend node + toolbar + config** — get the builder UI working\\n3. **Frontend validation** — enforce rules in compile step\\n4. **Backend circular reference check** — save-time safety\\n5. **Executor handler** — actual runtime execution with depth guard\\n6. **Delete protection** — prevent deleting templates referenced by others", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 100.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:20:27.433929+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:22:07.390317+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/195", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 291.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:22:07.474487+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T16:26:58.764929+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=I've reviewed the full PR diff. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation is solid and well-structured. Here's the summary:\\n\\n### What was done\\n1. **Backend**: Added `template` as a new node type with validation, circular reference detection (both direct self-reference and deep cycle detection via `_check_circular_refs`), and deletion protection for referenced templates.\\n2. **Slave/executor**: Added `_handle_template` for recursive execution of nested templates with depth limiting (max 5), shared context, and proper error propagation. Nested callbacks correctly prevent terminal status leaking from sub-templates.\\n3. **Web frontend**: New `TemplateNode` component, config panel support for selecting templates (filtering out the current template), a `ContextPanel` sidebar, compile/validate functionality with visual animation, and proper edge/reference cleanup on node deletion.\\n4. **Removed legacy code**: The hardcoded plan→develop→review state machine in `orchestrator.py` and `agent_prompts.py` were removed in favor of the graph executor, which is the right call.\\n\\n### Things I checked\\n- **Circular references**: Handled at three levels — schema validation (direct self-ref), DB-level recursive check on update, and runtime depth limit (5) in the executor. The `visited.discard(ref_id)` in `_check_circular_refs` correctly handles diamond patterns without false positives.\\n- **Error handling**: Template loader failures, missing templates, and nested execution failures all propagate correctly and don't crash the pipeline silently.\\n- **Security**: The template loader constructs its URL from the callback URL which is server-controlled, and uses the existing API key. No injection vectors.\\n- **Edge cases**: Delete protection prevents orphaned references. The `_fail_reason` pop in `_handle_template` prevents it from leaking to the parent scope. `_template_depth` is restored after execution.\\n- **Frontend consistency**: Template nodes follow the same patterns as existing node types for edge sync, reference cleanup, and config panel behavior.\\n\\nNo bugs, no security issues, no missing edge cases. The code is clean and consistent with the existing codebase patterns., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 44.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T16:26:58.817622+00:00", "completed