950	149	assistant	Here's the issue with iOS-side logging in PR #608:\n\n**The `postPlaybackLog` method in `AppDelegate.swift` sends logs to Dart via the `liveActivityChannel` using `invokeMethod("playbackLog", ...)`.** On the Dart side, `LiveActivityService` registers a handler for this:\n\n```dart\n_channel.setMethodCallHandler((call) async {\n  if (call.method == 'playbackLog') {\n    sl<PlaybackLogger>().ios(call.arguments as String);\n  }\n});\n```\n\n**The problem:** `LiveActivityService` sets `_channel.setMethodCallHandler()` inside its `init()` method. But `liveActivityChannel` on the iOS side is initialized in `application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)`, which runs **before** the Dart service locator and `LiveActivityService.init()` are called.\n\nThis means iOS logs sent during early lifecycle events (like `didEnterBackground` right after launch) will arrive before the Dart-side handler is registered. Those logs will be silently dropped — there's no `setMethodCallHandler` yet to receive them.\n\nAdditionally, `_channel.setMethodCallHandler()` **replaces** any existing handler. If `LiveActivityService` already had a method call handler registered elsewhere (for `handleLiveActivityCall` responses), this new handler would overwrite it. Looking at the code, the channel is used bidirectionally — Dart calls iOS methods on it, and now iOS also calls Dart on it. The `setMethodCallHandler` only handles `playbackLog` and ignores all other methods, so any future iOS→Dart calls on this channel would also be silently dropped.\n\n**Summary of issues:**\n1. **Race condition**: iOS `postPlaybackLog` fires before Dart's `setMethodCallHandler` is registered — early iOS logs are lost\n2. **Single handler limitation**: `setMethodCallHandler` can only have one handler per channel — setting it in `LiveActivityService.init()` could conflict if the channel needs to handle other iOS→Dart calls in the future	2026-03-08 13:25:39.2275+00
